<!--
  ============================================================================
  Warcasket_HazardRetune.xml                Jawa_Armoury · authored 2026-08-12
  ============================================================================

  ⚠️ NOT YET CONFIRMED IN GAME. Authored offline while the game was unavailable.
  NEXT_RELOAD.md "Armoury round 3" item 2 still asks for the live check that
  Hazard genuinely deflects everything a lightsaber throws. The numbers below are
  the owner's own recommendation from that entry; deploy is a separate decision.

  THE PROBLEM — one suit cancels both the weapon answer and the world
  ====================================================================
  VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard is immune to TWO different things at once, from two
  different mods, and neither author could see the other's contribution.

  Read 2026-08-12 from the live source, not from the def dump — the dump has NO
  file for these defs at all, because their XML element is the C# class name
  VFEPirates.WarcasketDef, not ThingDef:

    C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\294100\
      2723801948\...                            (VFE Pirates, load 470)
        <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
          <defName>VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard</defName>
          <statBases>
            <ArmorRating_Heat>2.0</ArmorRating_Heat>     <- MaxArmorRating
            <Insulation_Heat>72</Insulation_Heat>

    ...\3533261706\Patches\Insulation_Heat.xml   (Farhan's Tweaks, load 489)
        39 PatchOperationReplace ops, ALL rooted at
        /Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[...]:
            18 pieces -> Insulation_Heat  +5
            18 pieces -> Insulation_Heat +15
             3 pieces -> Insulation_Heat +333   <- shell, helmet, shoulders,
                                                   all three Hazard

  So, measured rather than asserted:

    ArmorRating_Heat 2.00 IS the engine's MaxArmorRating. Lightsabers and every
    other energy weapon do nothing. Next best shell is Barrage at 1.08.

    Insulation_Heat after Farhan, body shells only:
        Hazard        333      <- 22x the next best
        Shock / Siegebreaker / Guardian / Controller / Sarcophagus / Brute  15
        Warcasket / Marine / Recon / Cataphract / Aerial / Barrage           5

  On a desert world, for a faction whose entire designed drawback is being
  welded into steel in the heat, this single suit removes the weapon answer AND
  the environmental cost. It also undercuts the cortosis tier, which was meant
  to be THE rare answer to energy and has exactly one def (an armband).

  THE RETUNE
  ==========
  Keep Hazard the environmental specialist it is clearly meant to be; stop it
  being the answer to everything.

    ArmorRating_Heat  2.00 -> 1.30   still comfortably the best anti-energy suit
                                     in the load (Barrage, next, is 1.08), but a
                                     lightsaber now gets through.

    Insulation_Heat   333  -> 50 shell / 10 shoulders / 8 helmet
                                     68 total, ~4.5x the 15-point tier rather
                                     than 22x. Excellent hazmat, not weatherproof.
                                     The split keeps VFEP's own proportions
                                     (original 72 / 14 / 12).

  ⚠️ ONE NUMBER TO TURN. If 68 total still reads as too much on a desert map,
  change the shell op only — the helmet and shoulders are rounding.

  WHY THE XPATH LOOKS WRONG AND IS NOT
  ====================================
  The root is /Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef, NOT /Defs/ThingDef. A def's XML
  element name is its C# class, and these are WarcasketDefs, not ThingDefs — see
  traps.md. Farhan's 39 ops use exactly this form, which is independent
  confirmation. Sibling Armour_Ratings.xml caps the other 49 warcasket pieces
  and uses the same root; it excludes all three Hazard pieces by name so that
  this file is the only thing writing their ArmorRating_Heat.

  LOAD ORDER
  ==========
  farhanfair.warcaskettweakspatch  489
  mandrake.rsw.armoury            567   <- we replace his value, not the base

  Verified in runtime/backups/ModsConfig.full-568.2026-08-11.xml on 2026-08-12.
  If Farhan is ever moved after us, this patch silently loses and Hazard goes
  back to 333.

  SCOPE — NPC JUNKERS ARE THE POINT
  =================================
  Warcaskets can no longer be built by the player (Warcasket_BuildPathCut.xml),
  so every Hazard suit in the campaign is worn by someone shooting at you. That
  is precisely why the numbers still matter.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Dev-spawn a Hazard-suited Junker, hit it with a lightsaber: it should now
      TAKE DAMAGE. Before this patch it took none.
    * Inspect the suit: ArmorRating_Heat 130%, Insulation_Heat ~+68 °C total.
    * Cortosis armband should again be meaningfully better against energy.
    * `Could not resolve cross-reference` still at baseline 25.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- ArmorRating_Heat 2.00 -> 1.30, all three Hazard pieces -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
            <value><ArmorRating_Heat>1.30</ArmorRating_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
            <value><ArmorRating_Heat>1.30</ArmorRating_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard"]/statBases/ArmorRating_Heat</xpath>
            <value><ArmorRating_Heat>1.30</ArmorRating_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!--
          Insulation_Heat: undo Farhan's 333. Node is guaranteed to exist because
          his ops are PatchOperationReplace, which would already have failed
          loudly if it did not — but each op is still guarded, unlike his.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
            <value><Insulation_Heat>50</Insulation_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
            <value><Insulation_Heat>10</Insulation_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/statBases/Insulation_Heat</xpath>
            <value><Insulation_Heat>8</Insulation_Heat></value>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
